.TH GMODEM 1
.SH NAME
gmodem \- move files between two Flippers over RFID, Sub-GHz, NFC or BLE
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBgmodem send \-m\fR \fImedium\fR [\fB\-p\fR \fIpreset\fR] [\fB\-n\fR \fIrounds\fR] [\fB\-z\fR] [\fIfile\fR]
\fBgmodem recv \-m\fR \fImedium\fR [\fB\-p\fR \fIpreset\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIfile\fR] [\fB\-t\fR \fIsec\fR]
\fBgmodem chat \-m\fR \fImedium\fR [\fB\-p\fR \fIpreset\fR] [\fB\-f\fR \fImhz\fR]
\fBgmodem info\fR [\fB\-m\fR \fImedium\fR] [\fB\-p\fR \fIpreset\fR] [\fB\-f\fR \fImhz\fR]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Gmodem
sends a file from one Flipper to another that also runs Galtzagorriak
MINIX.
.I Medium
is
.BR rfid ,
.BR subghz ,
.B nfc
or
.BR ble .
Today
.B rfid
works; the others print "not implemented yet" and exit 2 until their
drivers can send (Sub-GHz: spec RP.8; NFC: Phase 13; BLE: Phase 15).
.PP
.B "RFID."
Hold the two Flippers back to back.
.B "gmodem send \-m rfid"
makes the Flipper a tag that plays the file over and over, in frames of
24 bytes, until Ctrl-C or
.I rounds
rounds;
.B "gmodem recv \-m rfid"
makes the other a reader that keeps every frame it has not got yet and
exits when the whole file is there, or after
.I sec
seconds (default 30) without a new frame.
Presets:
.B fast
(default) and
.BR robust .
One way only, a few tens of bytes a second.
The file to send may come from a pipe if it is at most 1 KB; the received
file goes to
.B \-o
.I file
or to standard output if that is a file (a pipe takes at most 1 KB).
.PP
.B "Compression."
.B "gmodem send \-z"
compresses the file first (heatshrink, LZSS) and sends the compressed
bytes; the receiver notices and unpacks them by itself, no option needed.
Text shrinks to a fifth or a third; photos, archives and random data grow
by up to 12 %, so
.B \-z
is off by default.
With
.B \-z
a pipe in or out may be bigger than 1 KB (it passes through
.BR /tmp ).
.PP
.B "Sub-GHz."
Presets
.BR narrow ,
.BR slow ,
.B std
(default),
.B wide
and
.BR max :
more bandwidth is faster and reaches less far.
Only frequencies and presets the region in
.B /etc/flipper/region
allows are used; in the EU the 433 and 868 MHz bands also limit the share
of time a transmitter may send (duty cycle).
.B "gmodem info \-m subghz"
shows what each preset does on the chosen frequency and whether it is
allowed.
.PP
Nothing is encrypted except over BLE: anyone near can receive it.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 everything arrived with a good CRC; 1 the transfer failed or timed out;
2 not possible here (usage, medium not there yet).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
gmodem recv \-m rfid \-o /tmp/notes.txt     # on the reader
gmodem send \-m rfid /home/flipper/notes.txt  # on the tag
gmodem send \-m rfid \-z /etc/rc            # text: about 3x faster
gmodem info \-m subghz \-f 869.85
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR rfid (1).
Spec section P; manual chapter "Data modems".
